In this issue, the problem surrounding telescope hinges will be described. Telescope hinges are hinges where the column is free to move in the axial direction. This leads to a new unknown, u_s, the column is free to move at the location of the hinge. This new unknown also comes with a new boundary condition, the axial force at location s has to be zero. A schematization of a telescope hinge applied to a 1D column object is shown below:

The influence of a telescope hinge can be applied to the load equation through a singularity function of order -2:
$$
u_s * ⟨ x - S ⟩ ^{-2}
$$
